me delivery rate is the one its customer contracts define.", "rules": ["A load is on time when the truck arrives at the final delivery stop at or before the end of the appointment window. Arriving early is on time.", "A load that arrived late and has a delay the shipper caused (a DLAY status event with reason SHPR) is left out of the measure, top and bottom. It is neither on time nor late.", "A load the shipper delayed that still arrived inside its window counts as on time.", "Arrival and appointment are compared on the same clock: local time at the facility.", "The rate is on-time loads divided by measured loads, over delivered loads.", "Two other meanings are in use and are not the official rate: operations watches arrival inside the appointment window for every delivered load, shipper-caused or not; and the customer portal uses its own rule."], "not_the_same_as": ["tw:PortalOnTime"], "warehouse_source": ["tms_stop: arr_ts, appt_end_lcl, tz_nm at the final delivery stop; tms_stat_evt: evt_cd = 'DLAY' with rsn_cd = 'SHPR'"]}]}}, {"seq": 3, "tool": "check_rule", "arguments": {"rule": "on-time"}, "response_id": "55d3be9d-c2a4-47c2-8926-81116661d1ed", "contract_version": "1.0.0", "result": {"rule": "on-time", "matches": [{"rule": "tw:DeliveredLoadShape", "statement": "A load is delivered when the carrier on its final row reports the final delivery: status DLVD. A canceled load does not count as delivered.", "applies_to": ["tw:DeliveredLoad"], "holds_in_current_data": true}, {"rule": "tw:InvoiceNeedsSignedProofShape", "statement": "A load can be invoiced only when a signed proof of delivery is on file. An unsigned document does not count.", "applies_to": ["tw:Invoice"], "holds_in_current_data": true}, {"rule": "tw:LoadBookedOnFirstTenderShape", "statement": "A load is booked on its first tender: the row that does not point to an earlier row. A re-tender is not a second load.", "applies_to": ["tw:Load"], "holds_in_current_data": true}, {"rule": "tw:TenderAccountsShape", "statement": "The account on a load is a shipping site, and the account that pays is a bill-to party. Neither is the customer.", "applies_to": ["tw:Tender"], "holds_in_current_data": true}]}}, {"seq": 4, "tool": "lookup_definition", "arguments": {"term": "rate"}, "response_id": "969e47f0-bd2c-4527-8a18-55a74bcd7c5e", "contract_version": "1.0.0", "result": {"term": "rate", "matches": [{"term": "tw:Currency", "kind": "business term", "label": "currency", "also_called": ["Canadian dollars", "US dollars", "cross-border", "exchange rate"], "definition": "Tessaway reports in US dollars.", "rules": ["Convert at the monthly rate in ref_fx_rate for the month of the document date: the invoice date, the credit date or the fee date.", "Costs on an invoiced load convert at the invoice month's rate.", "Most cross-border loads are rated, invoiced and paid in Canadian dollars. Every amount on such a load carries curr_cd = 'CAD' and is stored unconverted."], "warehouse_source": ["curr_cd on every amount; ref_fx_rate holds the monthly rate"]}, {"term": "tw:OnTime", "kind": "business term", "label": "on-time", "also_called": ["late", "late delivery", "on time", "on-time delivery rate", "on-time rate"], "definition": "Tessaway's official on-time delivery rate is the one its customer contracts define.", "rules": ["A load is on time when the truck arrives at the final delivery stop at or before the end of the appointment window. Arriving early is on time.", "A load that arrived late and has a delay the shipper caused (a DLAY status event with reason SHPR) is left out of the measure, top and bottom. It is neither on time nor late.", "A load the shipper delayed that still arrived inside its window counts as on time.", "Arrival and appointment are compared on the same clock: local time at the facility.", "The rate is on-time loads divided by measured loads, over delivered loads.", "Two other meanings are in use and are not the official rate: operations watches arrival inside the appointmen